    <div
      class="rapp-card rapp-mb16"
    >
      <div
        style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 12px;"
      >
        Your stats will appear here after your first study session.
      </div>
      <div
        style="font-size: 13px; color: rgb(58, 82, 70); line-height: 1.75;"
      >
        <p
          style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
        >
          <strong>
            Due today:
          </strong>
           cards whose next review date is today or earlier.
        </p>
        <p
          style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
        >
          <strong>
            Active cards:
          </strong>
           total cards with status Active (not archived or parked).
        </p>
        <p
          style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
        >
          <strong>
            Mature cards:
          </strong>
           cards with a stability value above the maturity threshold (default: 30 days). Mature cards need less frequent review.
        </p>
        <p
          style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
        >
          <strong>
            Recall accuracy:
          </strong>
           percentage of reviews rated Good or Easy in the last 30 days.
        </p>
        <p
          style="margin-bottom: 16px;"
        >
          <strong>
            Critical cards:
          </strong>
           cards with the stakes flag set. These are reviewed at higher priority.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="rapp-card rapp-mb16"
    >
      <div
        style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;"
      >
        How the scheduling works
      </div>
      <div
        style="font-size: 13px; color: rgb(58, 82, 70); line-height: 1.75;"
      >
        <p
          style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
        >
          The FSRS algorithm estimates the probability you will recall a card and schedules it to be reviewed just before that probability drops below a target threshold (default: 90%). Cards you recall easily are shown less often; cards you struggle with come back sooner.
        </p>
        <p>
          Reference: Open Spaced Repetition project, github.com/open-spaced-repetition.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="rapp-card rapp-mb20"
    >
      <div
        style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;"
      >
        What to expect
      </div>
      <div
        style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 12px; color: rgb(58, 82, 70);"
      >
        <div>
          <strong>
            Week 1:
          </strong>
           cards are new, intervals are short (1 to 3 days). High daily volume.
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>
            Week 4:
          </strong>
           familiar cards space out to 7 to 21 days. Daily workload stabilises.
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>
            Month 3:
          </strong>
           well-known cards reviewed once every few months. New cards drive most of the load.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
